/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  VMFL006.  NINE faceZones, one at each interior gate station x = 0.01 ... 0.09 m.
  THE TENTH STATION, x = 0.10 m, IS THE OUTLET PATCH ITSELF and needs no zone --
  the outlet boundary IS that plane exactly, so it is read with
  `regionType patch; name outlet;` in controlDict.  Using a faceZone there would
  ask a zone to carry boundary faces for no gain.

  WHY FACEZONES AND NOT A SAMPLED PLANE.  The gate quantity is the MASS-WEIGHTED
  (mixing-cup) average of the species mass fraction, which the manual defines on
  p.28 as "the mass-weighted average of the normalized species mass fraction A at
  x-locations".  A mixing cup is sum(phi*T)/sum(phi) over a cross-section, and phi
  -- the volumetric flux the solver actually conserves -- exists ONLY on real mesh
  faces.  Reading it on a faceZone therefore takes the solver's OWN conserved flux
  directly: no constructed geometry and no interpolation enters the gate.  A
  sampledSurface plane would have to interpolate, and an areaAverage would
  silently return the WRONG (area-weighted) statistic -- which is precisely the
  quantity this team measured to be 78 % away from the manual's numbers
  (PREREGISTRATION.md sec.3).

  blockMeshDict.template always uses an axial count that is a MULTIPLE OF 10 and
  UNIFORM axial spacing, so a mesh face lies exactly at each station on every
  level of the r = 2 family.  The box half-width 1e-6 m below is far smaller than
  half the finest cell (dx = 1.25e-4 m on L3), so exactly one face plane is
  captured per station -- and grade_vmfl006.py REFUSES if any zone's face count
  is not the level's radial cell count.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile
{
    version     2.0;
    format      ascii;
    class       dictionary;
    object      topoSetDict;
}

actions
(
    {
        name    f_x01;
        type    faceSet;
        action  new;
        source  boxToFace;
        box     (0.009999000 -1 -1) (0.010001000 1 1);
    }
    {
        name    x01;
        type    faceZoneSet;
        action  new;
        source  setToFaceZone;
        faceSet f_x01;
